    "_note": "2026-09-12 STRAT 11 = strat 25 approach + LIVE wrist-cam servo to the block CENTROID (tags 30-34 composed node-side), graded at the CENTRELINE tip, 4 cm ball / 5 s sustain / 40 s timeout_advance, keeps correcting through the hold (image-time wrist composition, no wrist-quiet gate). AIM POINT = block CENTROID + 3 cm up (centroid_standoff 0.03): [0.55, 0.04+col_y, 0.055] above the face, same column convention as strat 25/12, B3 = target_col_y 0.12. The servo nominal centroid is derived from this rung (target - centroid_standoff); servo_nominal is not used. Needs node --object_servo and tag_bridge --gripper --gripper-publish --object-tag-id 30,31,32,33,34. 2026-09-12b: servo_hold = camera-error HOLD INTEGRATOR (servo_hold_ki 0.3/s, per-rung cap 0.08 m): the twin parked the centreline tip 5 cm above the aim point (reach cost x0.27 vs Body Table Clearance); the integrator walks the target until the wrist cam sees the tip on centroid+standoff. Hold clock is camera-graded (fresh tag required), pad gate exempt. 2026-09-12c AIM AT THE CENTROID (user): reach_target_table = the CENTROID [0.55, 0.04+col_y, 0.025]; graded point = centreline tip + 0.045 m along the gripper approach axis (aim_centroid); Reach Level 1500 with reach_pitch_deg 45 (jaws lateral, nose 45 deg down) so the gripper POINTS at the block and the plates sit beside the centreline (no table-clearance fight). Accuracy = |tip + standoff*axis - centroid|, standoff stated. Standoff 0.045 (not 0.03): at 45 deg the block corner is 3.54 cm from the centroid along the axis, so 3 cm would put the tip inside the block edge; 4.5 cm leaves ~1 cm. 2026-09-12d: 45 deg / Reach Level 1500 / Reaching 300 FAILED on the twin (graded point 9-13 cm past the block for 30 s, Reach Level dominated, base crept, fall) -> the strat-9 hold recipe: reach_pitch_deg 30, Reach Level 1800, Reaching Hand Dist 1600 (hardware-certified holds 09-05..08). 2026-09-12h standoff 0.05 (was 0.045): at the achieved ~16-30 deg approach the tip sits on the block TOP PLANE at 5 cm (strat 12 B3 test dipped 2.6 cm below it and nudged the block 1.1 cm); 4.5 would be below the plane and the integrator would press the block. Same standoff as strat 12 -> the servo+integrator is the only difference. 2026-09-12j AIM FREE (user: \"the whole point was NOT pointing along a fixed axis; tags on every face; mimic strat 25\"): pitch/yaw pins removed (aim_free), Reach Level 600 = jaws-lateral roll only; the pointing comes from the aim_centroid graded point alone. Hover likewise roll-only. 2026-09-12k HARDWARE 12new_1: level gripper (pitch -4) hovered 6 cm high + 3 cm left AND the wrist cam lost tag 30 at the frame bottom (block 4 cm below the optical axis at 12 cm) -> pitch pinned 30 deg down, yaw aimed at the block (reach_level_aim=1), Reach Level 1800, standoff 0.06 (tip 0.5 cm above the top plane at 30 deg; 0.05 grazed the block in the twin). Hover rung stays roll-only. 2026-09-12l hardware: integrator cap 0.04 (real 12new_1/2: gripper pitch only 5-9 deg despite the 30 deg demand, tip sits ~5 cm high on the camera-housing table-clearance floor; do not let the integrator press the housing into the slab). 2026-09-12o HOVER RUNG REMOVED (user: go straight like strat 25, no staging in front); 9 rungs again, aim rung = kf 3.",
